WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:08.136
Hi! Today you learn: mein, dein, sein, ihr.

2
00:00:08.536 --> 00:00:10.944
Whose is this?

3
00:00:12.633 --> 00:00:17.513
Each person has a word. Listen:

4
00:00:17.913 --> 00:00:20.489
I: my dog

5
00:00:20.889 --> 00:00:23.537
you: your dog

6
00:00:23.937 --> 00:00:26.561
he: his dog

7
00:00:26.961 --> 00:00:29.585
she: her dog

8
00:00:29.985 --> 00:00:32.921
we: our dog

9
00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:39.057
Careful! This is Tom's dog:

10
00:00:39.457 --> 00:00:41.817
That's his dog.

11
00:00:42.217 --> 00:00:45.249
And this is Anna's dog:

12
00:00:45.649 --> 00:00:48.225
That's her dog.

13
00:00:48.625 --> 00:00:54.225
In Spanish you say su for both. Not in German!

14
00:00:55.933 --> 00:01:01.725
Like ein and eine: with die and the plural you add an e:

15
00:01:02.125 --> 00:01:04.221
my brother

16
00:01:04.621 --> 00:01:06.957
my sister

17
00:01:07.357 --> 00:01:09.477
my car

18
00:01:09.877 --> 00:01:12.285
my parents

19
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.416
Listen: Lena is tidying up.

20
00:01:17.816 --> 00:01:20.248
Is this your key?

21
00:01:20.648 --> 00:01:25.432
Yes, thanks! It's mine.

22
00:01:25.832 --> 00:01:28.000
And the jacket?

23
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.000
That's Anna's jacket.

24
00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.096
Ah, her jacket!

25
00:01:34.496 --> 00:01:36.568
Exactly.

26
00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:45.739
Now you! Show three things and say: Das ist mein… or Das ist meine…

27
00:01:53.433 --> 00:01:57.569
Great! Now you can:

28
00:01:57.969 --> 00:02:04.217
You say who something belongs to – with mein, dein, sein and ihr.

29
00:02:04.617 --> 00:02:06.737
See you soon!
